# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_6775> (<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_6775>)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_6775> "A monohydroxybenzoic acid that is salicylic acid substituted by an amino group at the 5-position. Mesalazine, also known as mesalamine or 5-aminosalicylic acid (5-ASA), is a medication used to treat inflammatory bowel disease, including ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_6775> "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism")
