# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000021> (<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000021>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16489364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27439371") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000021> "The central nervous system agents are medicines that affect the central nervous system (CNS). There are many different types of drugs that work on the CNS, including anesthetics, anticonvulsants, antiemetics, antiparkinson agents, CNS stimulants, muscle relaxants, narcotic analgesics (pain relievers), nonnarcotic analgesics (such as acetaminophen and NSAIDs), and sedatives. Features of CNS drugs are related to their ability to penetrate the blood-brain barrier affinity and exhibit CNS activity and can be used in the management of neuro degenerative and psychiatric problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000021> "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000021> "HMDM:0000021")
