# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000094> (<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000094>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21417217") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000094> "Lyases are enzymes that catalyze the bond construction and breaking by means other than hydrolysis or redox reactions. Such enzymes are particular in the sense that they only require one substrate for the reaction in one direction, but two substrates for the reverse reaction.")
