# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000097> (<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000097>)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000097> "Cytochrome (CYP) enzymes catalyze the metabolic reactions of endogenous and exogenous compounds. The superfamily of enzymes is found across many organisms, regardless of type, except for plants. Differences in cytochrome subunits are expected to be critical in deciding the unique substrates that allow this functional diversity.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000097> "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism")
