# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000902> (<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000902>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37157031") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HMDM_0000902> "The apg is an acarbose-preferred glucosidase that was discovered in intestinal bacteria from patients with Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) chronic metabolic disease. The Apg hydrolyses acarbose into small molecules (acarviosine-glucose and acarviosine) with loss of inhibitor function to porcine pancreatic amylase and is widely distributed in human intestinal microorganisms, especially in Klebsiella.")
